    "q-134737": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134737",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=0.75x+2.25.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=8$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $11.25?$",
      "worked_solution": "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =0.75x+2.25 \\\\  & =0.75(8)+2.25 \\\\  & =8.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =11.25-8.25 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
