    "q-134736": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134736",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A veterinarian collects data on a puppy's height $y$ (in inches) at certain times $x$ (in months) since it was born. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=2.2x+3.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual after $5$ months if the actual height of the $5$-month old puppy is $15.5\\,in?$",
      "worked_solution": "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated height using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =2.2x+3.5 \\\\  & =2.2(5)+3.5 \\\\  & =14.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =15.5-14.5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $1\\,in.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
