    "q-134788": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134788",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14233881/assets/f940a05c937b3158ce737959dee4685d216e6d55d6651672aa910cdb2c492f1e.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?",
      "worked_solution": "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(5,1).$ So, our actual value is $y=1.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=5$ has the $y$-coordinate $0.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14233881/assets/937c0307a74881c87e6a33c47b32a1ac2d5124326b13538455640cd9fc88c14e.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
