    "q-134812": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134812",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14233881/assets/243a4212d1128a79203493bf672ad1c956fe0f48aad6abbb910de2861d99669c.png)\n\nA dog food company records data on the number of dogs $(x)$ sheltered at some kennels across the country and the corresponding amount of dog food $y$ (in kilograms) consumed in a month. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above. \n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted data point?",
      "worked_solution": "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(10,175).$ So, our actual value is $y=175.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=10$ has the $y$-coordinate $200.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=200.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14233881/assets/2cd59a9ae9c7ad474a9d5a308d4b8f3c9b96be70acdf1e3613dfc4757ff01766.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =175-200 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $-25\\,kg.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
